Z||000004||BroCar 87||07-17-2000||11:10 PM||||Here is a pic of mine... i have a little bit more room in the passenger area, enough to easily fit one of my friends in with no complaints (if there is such a thing as a friend not complaining)! Well I have foot room open on the left and about 12 inches in between the seat and the speaker...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/inspk1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||07-17-2000||11:37 PM||||I'm tellin ya Bro, bust out with the fiberglass and make that sucker sit back in there! I know you can do it!<BR>My 10" sits flush with the footrest. My passenger has more legroom then I do! And no steering wheel in the way!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Majik||07-17-2000||11:59 PM||||I hear a lot of talk about the sub in the footrest area...with the size of the car, and the amount of room the base wave takes to expand, how loud do those things sound?  <BR>I'm planning on installing duel 4inchers in the dash on both sides, and a 6incher in the column...with tweeters around...powered by a 4x75 watt amp.  Wondering if adding a sub down in that lil foot hole area is really worth it.<BR>Stimpy, may have to stop by over there in OKC to see how you did yours!  <P>Majik<BR>also, off subject, anyone have any new pontiac head units laying around (with cd)?  will post down in the buy/sell area.||||reg||5
Z||000007||Homicidal||07-18-2000||12:06 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.members.home.net/lov/images/Mvc-003s.jpg"> <P>Spot MY box!  Hehe, right behind my seat!  It's a Polk 10" db series so it doesn't need a box much bigger than the actual sub itself!<P>Passenger has all the legroom, and since I am not a big guy (5'7") it's PERFECT!<P>The way it faces the firewall with a small 1" spacer in between it makes it a virtual bandpass!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||07-18-2000||12:25 AM||||Majik, just like homicidal I use a Polk 10, mine is the dX, just a slightly updated version of h's db. They have the ability to handle some respectable power and still use the small enclosure. I am driving mine w/ a 440w amp bridged mono and believe me, it pounds. Turning the volume past midway turns the rearview mirror into a blur, and maxing out before distortion will cause the sides of my nostrils to quiver in sympathy with the beat. Yeah, it works!<P>As far as how to make one, I was very pleased at how easy it was to make. The key is to use a high quality speaker that is specially designed for small enclosures. I endorse Polk. My dX10 is freakin bulletproof! That small airspace would shred a cheap speaker in no time.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TheFiero64||07-18-2000||11:59 AM||||I made my own. I took a bass cannon and cut it to about 6 1/2 inches long and mounted it in the stock location. It has a 100 watt amp that came with the cannon and I put it in the stock amp location. It has good hard hitting bass. I want to add a cross tube like the stock one on the top to see if it gets even more bass because it doesn't hit as hard with the roof off and the windows down.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jul18^04.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jul18^07.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
